WEBVTT

00:00:05.339 --> 00:00:10.939
<v Callum Reid>Morning, all. Monday the ninth, and it's still raining sideways. Anyone actually manage their weekend plans?</v>

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:19.039
<v Jamie Brennan>Planned a walk. Got as far as the car, saw the weather, went back in. Very successful weekend, really.</v>

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:22.489
<v Tomasz Nowak>Good preventative maintenance on your boots.</v>

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:29.010
<v Callum Reid>Exactly. I stood beside a football pitch getting soaked. Yours sounds better, Jamie.</v>

00:00:31.219 --> 00:00:34.369
<v Hannah Price>Are we all on? Teams says someone's still connecting.</v>

00:00:35.579 --> 00:00:40.479
<v Olumide Adeyemi>That's me twice. Phone's in, laptop's thinking about it. You can hear me, yeah?</v>

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:45.979
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, you're fine. Right, quick run through what's already finished first.</v>

00:00:48.399 --> 00:00:53.649
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Already swapped the filter on the tower yesterday. That's done, not something for this morning.</v>

00:00:54.149 --> 00:00:57.299
<v Tomasz Nowak>That was the one showing on the old handover?</v>

00:00:58.609 --> 00:01:01.060
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, same one. Old entry, finished job.</v>

00:01:02.969 --> 00:01:08.920
<v Jamie Brennan>And I already swapped the filter on the GT2 water valve yesterday. That one's done as well.</v>

00:01:10.969 --> 00:01:16.569
<v Priya Raman>While we're on old entries, I signed off the inspection on the water ring on Tuesday.</v>

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:22.079
<v Hannah Price>Last Tuesday, yeah? So that's a completed inspection, not one waiting on us.</v>

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:27.280
<v Priya Raman>Exactly. Signed off. Don't put it back in the pile.</v>

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:38.620
<v Callum Reid>Different thing on the water ring, though. Boss, if you've got a spare minute, can you book a contractor to look at the water ring by 11am?</v>

00:01:40.599 --> 00:01:47.950
<v Sarah Okafor>I can't take that, sorry. I'm tied up on the production side this morning; I'd only end up sitting on it.</v>

00:01:49.599 --> 00:01:54.500
<v Jamie Brennan>Is that the booking needed by eleven, rather than someone physically here by eleven?</v>

00:01:56.909 --> 00:02:05.659
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, the booking. Jamie, can you take that instead—book a contractor to look at the water ring by 11am, if you've got a spare minute?</v>

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:12.389
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, I'll take it off boss. I'll book a contractor to look at the water ring by 11am.</v>

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:20.479
<v Priya Raman>And just to separate those two things, my inspection being signed off doesn't mean this contractor booking's already done.</v>

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:25.610
<v Jamie Brennan>Understood. Booking's mine; I'm not reopening your inspection.</v>

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:29.050
<v Callum Reid>Right. Anything to add on the new starters?</v>

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:39.259
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, I'll sort the training records for the new starters. That's in the whenever you get a chance category, but I'll have them ready tomorrow at 9:30.</v>

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:43.180
<v Hannah Price>Cheers, boss. Tomorrow at 9:30 for the records, then.</v>

00:02:45.289 --> 00:02:48.090
<v Sarah Okafor>That's it. Not making it a drop-everything job.</v>

00:02:49.379 --> 00:02:56.729
<v Callum Reid>Access-wise, we can't get to the Atlas until production gives us a window. Still blocked, no work on that agreed here.</v>

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:01.900
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right, so it's not secretly available because it's Monday?</v>

00:03:04.229 --> 00:03:10.879
<v Callum Reid>Sadly not. And we can't get to the desiccant unit until production gives us a window either. Same blocker.</v>

00:03:12.409 --> 00:03:16.960
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, without a window there's nothing to get into on either of those.</v>

00:03:18.699 --> 00:03:22.550
<v Callum Reid>Exactly. Just carrying the blockers, not handing either job out today.</v>

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:30.210
<v Olumide Adeyemi>One observation from me: heard a slight rattle from the big valve by the gate, nothing to action yet.</v>

00:03:32.289 --> 00:03:35.439
<v Tomasz Nowak>Just a noise you've noticed, not a strip-down request?</v>

00:03:36.949 --> 00:03:39.750
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Just the observation. Nothing to action yet, honestly.</v>

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:50.430
<v Callum Reid>There's also downtime to schedule with production for the door switch on two. Low priority, needs scheduling by the 28th. That hasn't got an owner.</v>

00:03:52.449 --> 00:03:58.050
<v Sarah Okafor>That's agreeing the downtime with production, rather than saying the switch work itself is due then?</v>

00:03:59.409 --> 00:04:05.710
<v Callum Reid>Yeah. Schedule downtime for the door switch on two with production by the 28th. That's the outstanding bit.</v>

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:13.759
<v Tomasz Nowak>I can't volunteer for the scheduling side. Don't put my name against it just because I mentioned the handover.</v>

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:19.990
<v Callum Reid>No, fair. Nobody's taken that, so it stays unowned. Low priority, but still needs doing.</v>

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:29.839
<v Callum Reid>For my bit, I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the Arburg by the end of the week. That's fairly important.</v>

00:04:32.259 --> 00:04:36.110
<v Tomasz Nowak>Cheers, Cal. Permit to work and isolation both with you, then?</v>

00:04:38.269 --> 00:04:42.819
<v Callum Reid>Yep, both with me for the Arburg. By the end of the week.</v>

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:49.959
<v Hannah Price>Okay, so that commitment's the permit and isolation, not a general promise that every job on it is finished.</v>

00:04:50.279 --> 00:04:54.480
<v Callum Reid>Correct. Let's not accidentally promise the whole factory while we're at it.</v>

00:04:55.889 --> 00:05:00.790
<v Callum Reid>Pri, can you investigate the pressure drop on the air compressor today at 2pm?</v>

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:06.350
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, I'll investigate the pressure drop on the air compressor today at 2pm.</v>

00:05:07.399 --> 00:05:11.600
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Investigation, yeah? We're not calling it a failed part at this stage.</v>

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:17.550
<v Priya Raman>No, exactly. It's a pressure drop to investigate, not a replacement I've already decided on.</v>

00:05:18.949 --> 00:05:25.600
<v Tomasz Nowak>Sorry, I was talking over you there. That's what I was going to say—bit early to name a part.</v>

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:32.040
<v Priya Raman>Yeah. Otherwise we end up diagnosing it by committee over a crackly microphone.</v>

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:37.410
<v Callum Reid>All right. Today at 2pm for that, Pri. Keeping that time as agreed.</v>

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:39.670
<v Priya Raman>Yep, two today.</v>

00:05:40.769 --> 00:05:48.819
<v Hannah Price>Just checking I followed the water ring bit with the audio cutting out. Completed inspection and a new contractor booking are separate entries?</v>

00:05:50.699 --> 00:05:54.899
<v Priya Raman>Yes. Inspection signed off on Tuesday, finished. No repeat inspection agreed here.</v>

00:05:55.389 --> 00:06:00.990
<v Jamie Brennan>And I've accepted the contractor booking for the water ring, by 11am. That's the live one.</v>

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:09.920
<v Sarah Okafor>And training records for the new starters are mine, tomorrow at 9:30. The whenever you get a chance one, not an urgent escalation.</v>

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:18.930
<v Callum Reid>Good. I've got the fairly important permit to work and isolation for the Arburg, by the end of the week.</v>

00:06:19.589 --> 00:06:24.839
<v Tomasz Nowak>That's clear. Atlas and desiccant unit still blocked, so neither's suddenly appeared on my list.</v>

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:29.389
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And my tower filter's finished. Rattle was information only. That's me.</v>

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:35.519
<v Hannah Price>Fine from quality. Much easier when finished work doesn't keep coming round again.</v>

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:41.310
<v Jamie Brennan>Like my weekend walk. Still pending, depending on the weather.</v>

00:06:43.269 --> 00:06:46.769
<v Callum Reid>Not putting a deadline on that. We'd never hit it.</v>

00:06:47.290 --> 00:06:50.089
<v Sarah Okafor>You'd need a production window and a waterproof.</v>

00:06:50.629 --> 00:07:00.079
<v Callum Reid>Last thing for clarity: scheduling downtime with production for the door switch on two stays unowned, low priority, by the 28th. Nobody's accepted it in this meeting.</v>

00:07:00.430 --> 00:07:02.180
<v Callum Reid>Right, that's us. Thanks, everyone.</v>
